WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.727
Most business slideshows need more than music.

2
00:00:03.727 --> 00:00:09.381
Photos of a kitchen, a car, or a product cannot tell a viewer the price, the size,

3
00:00:09.381 --> 00:00:10.553
or the next step.

4
00:00:10.553 --> 00:00:15.917
That is the job of a voiceover, with music sitting quietly underneath.

5
00:00:15.917 --> 00:00:21.003
Choose instrumental tracks, because lyrics compete with narration.

6
00:00:21.003 --> 00:00:26.919
Set the music roughly fifteen to twenty decibels below the voice while it speaks,

7
00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:29.768
and let it rise slightly in the pauses.

8
00:00:29.768 --> 00:00:35.951
Pick a calm, steady tempo for property or vehicle listings, something lighter for

9
00:00:35.951 --> 00:00:39.463
products, and nearly invisible for explainers.

10
00:00:39.463 --> 00:00:45.460
Use only music whose licence covers every platform where the video will appear, and

11
00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:46.905
keep a record of it.

12
00:00:46.905 --> 00:00:52.101
Caption every narrated slideshow, because captions carry the whole message for

13
00:00:52.101 --> 00:00:57.631
viewers watching with the sound off, and they are required for accessibility at the

14
00:00:57.631 --> 00:01:00.163
basic level of web content guidelines.
